Licensor: DAI-KOMIO e.K. (tyrosec), Ahrensfelde, Germany – info@tyrosec.com

1. Purpose. The source code of the tyrosec agent is published so that customers and interested parties can review what
   a program with far-reaching privileges does on their servers, and verify that the officially published, signed
   binaries are built from exactly this source. Publication is not a grant of general use. This is not open-source
   software.

2. Permitted without separate consent.
   2.1 Review. Any natural or legal person – including a company, e.g. before or during a contract with tyrosec – may
       read, review and analyse the software, have it reviewed by commissioned third parties (e.g. auditors), and
       compile it in order to compare the resulting binaries with the officially published binaries. Binaries built
       this way may only be used for that comparison, not run. Security issues may be reported to the licensor (see
       SECURITY.md).
   2.2 Private use. A natural person may compile, run and modify the software on devices or servers they own or rent
       themselves, solely for purposes unrelated to any commercial or professional activity.

3. Beyond section 2, the following in particular requires the licensor's prior written consent: (a) any distribution
   of the software or binaries built from it, modified or not, and making modified versions publicly available; (b) any
   use by or for companies, self-employed persons, freelancers, associations, public authorities or other
   organisations, including internal use, beyond review under section 2.1 – in particular running self-built binaries;
   (c) any use on behalf of third parties, in particular monitoring or managing other people's servers, offering it as
   a service or as part of a hosting offering; (d) incorporating the software or parts of it into other software or
   products; (e) using the software or parts of it to train or improve artificial-intelligence models; the licensor
   expressly reserves text and data mining (reservation under section 44b(3) of the German Copyright Act); (f) removing
   or altering copyright, licence or trademark notices.

4. Customers use the agent via the officially published, signed binaries under the tyrosec terms and conditions; this
   licence does not extend them.
5. Mandatory statutory rights, in particular under sections 69d and 69e of the German Copyright Act, remain unaffected.
6. No rights to tyrosec names, logos or trademarks are granted.
7. For the free uses permitted under section 2 the software is provided without warranty; liability is limited to
   intent and gross negligence and to mandatory statutory liability.
8. Any breach of this licence terminates the rights under section 2 with immediate effect.
9. German law applies, excluding the UN Convention on Contracts for the International Sale of Goods. For merchants and
   public-law entities the place of jurisdiction is the licensor's registered office. If any provision is invalid, the
   remaining provisions remain unaffected.

